Design attribution
-------------------
eggswap's design is informed by realiti4/claude-swap
(https://github.com/realiti4/claude-swap), which is MIT licensed. Two ideas
were taken from studying that project, in concept only, and reimplemented
independently here:

  1. The technique of binding a single Claude CLI process to one account by
     setting the CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR environment variable per process, so that
     concurrent processes on one machine do not share (and corrupt) one
     account's session state.
  2. The general shape of a per-account quota/capacity model: tracking usage
     against a named account so that a scheduler can pick among several
     accounts rather than always using the same one.

No code, file, string, or configuration from claude-swap is present in this
repository. eggswap's actual types, algorithms, and CLI are its own, built to
this project's own honesty and fencing contract (see eggswap/core/types.py).

